<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    The mech stun pulse's display, the centerEffecter of the armor's
    CompProperties_MechStunPulse (ThingDefs_Misc/Warcasket_Overlord.xml): Biotech's
    BlastMechBandShockwave (1.7.5013, Biotech Defs/Effects/Effecter_Misc.xml), the
    explosionCenterEffecter of the MechBandShockwave damage def, with its three flecks swapped
    for copies of our own. OverlordWarcasket.CompMechStunPulse plays it in place of Biotech's
    (its header has how).

    Biotech's is one size, the apocriton's, whatever the radius of the explosion: vanilla
    spawns it at scale 1 and nothing in it reads the radius. Ours shrinks with the pulse, by
    the pulse's radius over the armor's centerEffecterRadius (30.9, the apocriton's), so a pulse
    of a third the apocriton's reach is drawn a third the size and one of the same reach is
    the apocriton's exactly. It is not sized to the cells the pulse stuns, as the apocriton's
    is not either: it keeps the apocriton's proportion to them.

    The values here are the apocriton's and are never what plays. At startup and whenever the
    settings window closes, StunPulseSetting multiplies each child's scale, and the growthRate
    of each child's fleck, by that ratio:
    - scale is where a fleck or mote starts: left at 1 on the three flecks, as Biotech's, and
      24 on the red flash, a mote that does not grow.
    - A fleck's growth is added to its scale each second whatever scale it was spawned at
      (FleckStatic.TimeInterval, 1.7.5013 and 1.6 decompiles), so the scale alone would shrink
      where the wave and the ring start and not how far they spread. Their growthRate has to
      shrink with it, which is why the flecks are our own: the write would otherwise land on
      Biotech's, and on the apocriton's pulse with them.
    How long each part lasts is untouched, so the display plays in the apocriton's time, and so
    is the sound, the damage def's.

    The four children, in Biotech's order, with their size across at the apocriton's radius
    and at the shipped 9.9:
    - OLWC_MechStunPulseWave, the distortion wave: 21 cells growing to 51, 6.7 to 16 at 9.9.
    - OLWC_MechStunPulseRing, the red line: 6 cells growing to 143, 1.9 to 46 at 9.9.
    - OLWC_MechStunPulseFlash, the red glow at the centre: 16 cells shrinking to nothing, 5.1.
    - Mote_RedFlashStrong, Biotech's own, the flash over it: 24 cells, 7.7.
    Those are the sizes of the quads; the line sits inside its texture.

    The rest of an explosion's display is sized by the radius already, the white flash, the
    smoke and the camera shake, and the electric arcs spark on cells the pulse reaches.
  -->
  <EffecterDef>
    <defName>OLWC_MechStunPulse</defName>
    <children>
      <li>
        <subEffecterClass>SubEffecter_SprayerTriggered</subEffecterClass>
        <fleckDef>OLWC_MechStunPulseWave</fleckDef>
        <burstCount>1</burstCount>
        <spawnLocType>OnSource</spawnLocType>
        <absoluteAngle>true</absoluteAngle>
        <rotation>0~0</rotation>
      </li>
      <li>
        <subEffecterClass>SubEffecter_SprayerTriggered</subEffecterClass>
        <fleckDef>OLWC_MechStunPulseRing</fleckDef>
        <burstCount>1</burstCount>
        <spawnLocType>OnSource</spawnLocType>
        <absoluteAngle>true</absoluteAngle>
        <rotation>0~0</rotation>
      </li>
      <li>
        <subEffecterClass>SubEffecter_SprayerTriggered</subEffecterClass>
        <fleckDef>OLWC_MechStunPulseFlash</fleckDef>
        <burstCount>1</burstCount>
        <spawnLocType>OnSource</spawnLocType>
        <absoluteAngle>true</absoluteAngle>
        <rotation>0~0</rotation>
      </li>
      <li>
        <subEffecterClass>SubEffecter_SprayerTriggered</subEffecterClass>
        <moteDef>Mote_RedFlashStrong</moteDef>
        <burstCount>1</burstCount>
        <spawnLocType>OnSource</spawnLocType>
        <scale>24</scale>
      </li>
    </children>
  </EffecterDef>
</Defs>
